  "limits": [
    "Entity comparison is a two-live-entity success workload, not equivalent unrestricted APIs. Both validate actual DSparse handles; the archetype adapter also stages a whole world and uses its actual versioned cache.",
    "Sparse component sets are original benchmark code with dense values/inverse maps. The scalar dictionary oracle checks each whole workload checksum independently.",
    "Exactly6000 mutations and1/16/256 queries per mutation; timings include state publication and query-cache maintenance. No deletion/reuse in this timing workload; those have separate semantic tests.",
    "RC alternatives reclaim the same15-node/eight-owned-leaf tree;1000 reconstructions occur outside each timer, but clock overhead remains in the accumulated duration.",
    "Region integer tree versus RC owned-text tree census is structural accounting, not a fair comparative cleanup latency benchmark.",
    "Seven host trials, no affinity/frequency control, no universal performance or hard real-time guarantee. Static stack reports exclude runtime/caller stack and require interpretation."
  ]
}
